src/gunyahvm/macos_vendor/ holds Droid-VM/macOS-DroidVM assembly scripts
(kernel collection linking, APFS volumes, data store, device tree), with
packed_ramdisk.py from Droid-VM/UniXNU, adapted only for package imports.
src/gunyahvm/macos_aea.py follows the Apple Encrypted Archive format as
implemented by blacktop/ipsw (MIT), reimplemented in Python.

No Apple software, firmware, kernel collection, disk or guest image is
distributed: each device downloads the macOS files it needs from Apple and
assembles them locally.

* Casilda 1.4.0, Juan Pablo Ugarte and contributors, LGPL-2.1-only:
  https://gitlab.gnome.org/jpu/casilda
  The upstream source archive and Jonathan Carter's Debian packaging are
  pinned in third_party/casilda/source.json. Original authors and COPYING
  remain intact. The separate touch patch forwards GTK touch sequences to
  the upstream Wayland seat. The buffer lifetime patch keeps client DMA-BUFs
  locked until GTK releases their textures. The keyboard focus patch propagates
  GTK focus changes to Wayland clients. Casilda uses wlroots 0.20 and the distribution's
  GTK; neither is forked.
